A set named after a predeclared identifier (int) is rejected outright: a top-level
func int would shadow the builtin for the whole destination package. The rejection
is by the set name alone, independent of the signature (here int also appears in a
func-typed parameter, but that is irrelevant to the diagnostic).
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrShadowsPredeclared
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}

//plumb:int
func Use(f func(int) int) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
